A||N||8||FieroMorg||84 SE no start!||||1||
Z||000000||FieroMorg||03-29-2000||11:42 AM||||Ok everybody, here's my situation......<P>I got the 84 SE out of the garage 2 weeks ago... started on the first try.... I let it run for about 15 minutes, backed it into the garage and shut it down... This weekend I go to start it up and nothin at all....doesn't even crank over....ok.. so I check the battery and it's fine...... so I'm stumped...and I'm not mechanically inclined at all so any suggestions where to look next would be helpful...<P>Thanks<BR>Morgan||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||03-29-2000||01:34 PM||||Clean the battery cables terminals, check your ground wires and check the little wire that runs from the positive terminal.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroMorg||03-29-2000||01:42 PM||||Batboy....<P>There is power running in the car....battery gauge says it's ok...<P>Morgan||||reg||1
Z||000003||85fierose||03-29-2000||03:44 PM||||Is there any noise at all when you turn the key such as a click? When you turn the key to the on positon can you hear the fuel pump kick in? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||03-29-2000||03:48 PM||||A couple of ideas...<P>Automatic - check Park/Neutral switch. If it's bad sometimes you can get it to start by shifting to Neutral. <P>Stick - Check the clutch switch. The switch is mounted on the clutch pedal. If not working, it's usually just out of adjustment. Can unplug and jumper wires to test.||||reg||3
Z||000005||FieroMorg||03-29-2000||03:49 PM||||85fierose...<P>Yes I can hear the fuel pump going.....<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||03-29-2000||05:23 PM||||You may have enough juice to run the electrical stuff, but not enough to turn over the starter, they take a lot of amps. Once with my Suburban, I stopped for gas and went to start up again and got nothing, not even a click. Gauges worked, I turned on the headlights, they worked. Tried jump starting it, still nothing. Yanked the side post battery terminals off, cleaned them, and screwed them back on. It fired right up after that.||||reg||1
Z||000007||daved||03-30-2000||12:25 AM||||Morg,  Like to help...I'm not too far from you...your in Listowel, right?. I'm in Forest so not too far. <BR> If you do all above, and a jump doesnt help ( to eliminate a weak battery), then its pointing to the starter, or the wiring to it, as the problem.  Note the symptoms and post what you find.  I sent you ICQ this pm and got no reply, Try sending to me # 58482286, Dave||||reg||1
